{"availability":"available","full":"dguywhoknows/adaptive-trivia","name":"adaptive-trivia","description":"Adaptive AI trivia where questions and players both carry Elo ratings, so every question lands at the edge of what you know.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-07T04:13:28Z","updated":"2026-10-17T04:49:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/adaptive-trivia/","topics":["elo-rating","game","github-pages","javascript","trivia"],"demo":"https://dguywhoknows.github.io/adaptive-trivia/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-20T04:02:31.997Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-20T04:02:31.997Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-20T04:02:31.997Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:04:18.336Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-15T23:47:31.144Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-20T04:02:31.997Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Adaptive AI trivia where questions and players both carry Elo ratings, so every question lands at the edge of what you know.","Trivia Elo matches you with questions the way chess servers match opponents. You have an overall rating and one per category, and every question has its own rating too. Each answer updates both sides with the Elo formula, so the question bank calibrates itself from real play. The picker aims for a 60% expected win rate to keep you in the flow zone. When good matches run low, the AI generates fresh, non-repeating questions near your level in the background. A built-in bank of 36 hand-checked questions lets it work fully offline."],"features":["Dual Elo: per-player (overall + per-category) and per-question ratings, both updated every answer","Target-difficulty picker that aims for 60% success with a little randomness","Background AI question generation near your rating, de-duplicated against the pool","20-second timer, keyboard play (1-4, Enter), streaks",